-- title:
--   Crossing presentation at a τ₀-stable end of the blown-up chart
-- statement:
--   **Arithmetic data.** Fix a prime $q$ and an integer $M'\neq 0$ with $q\nmid M'$ (`hqM'`), and a prime $\ell$ with $\ell\equiv 11\pmod{12}$ (`hℓ12`) and $\ell\mid M'$ (`hℓM'`). Let $L$ be a field of characteristic $0$ and $\zeta\in L$ a primitive $q$-th root of unity (`hζ`), and assume (`hι`) that some ring homomorphism $L\to\mathbb C$ carries $\zeta$ to $e^{2\pi i/q}$. Let $H_1\le(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times$ be, by `hH₁`, the intersection of [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH q M'`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L22), i.e. the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q)^\times$ (the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$), with the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/\ell)^\times$. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L\subseteq L((t))$ which, by `hK`, is [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.xHFunctionField (q^2*M') H₁)`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103): the subfield generated over $L$ by the coefficientwise image in $L((t))$ of the $q$-expansion function field over $\mathbb Q$ attached to $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$.
--
--   Let $A$ be a Henselian discrete valuation ring with fraction field $L$ and algebraically closed residue field, with $q\in\mathfrak m_A$ (`hAq`) and $\zeta$ in the image of $A\to L$ (`hζA`), and let $K$ be an $A$-algebra compatibly with $A\to L\to K$. Let $j\in K$ be nonzero with Laurent expansion the coefficientwise image of [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) (`hj`), let $\varpi$ generate $\mathfrak m_A$ (`hϖ`), and let $\varpi_t\in A$ satisfy $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1}=q\cdot(\text{unit})$ (`hϖt`). Write $C:=$ `chartAlgFin A K j` for the $A$-subalgebra of elements of $K$ integral over $A[j]$, and $X:=$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) for the two-chart integral model, the pushout of $\operatorname{Spec}C$ and $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the chart algebra at $j^{-1}$ along the middle chart, with its structure morphism `toBase` to $\operatorname{Spec}A$.
--
--   Let $y\subset C$ be a maximal ideal (`hy`) containing $\varpi$ (`hϖy`) which is supersingular in the sense of `hss`: for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi:C\to\Omega$ with kernel $y$, the value $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), the set of those $j$-invariants for which every elliptic curve over $\Omega$ with that invariant has no nonzero $q$-torsion point.
--
--   **The Drinfeld-chart rigidity hypothesis.** The hypothesis `hArig` asserts, for every point $z$ of $X$ at which the germ $\varpi_z$ of $\varpi$ (pulled back along `toBase`, `hϖz`) lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk (`hz`), and every point $y'$ of $\operatorname{Spec}C$ mapping to $z$ (`hy'`) which is supersingular in the above sense (`hss'`), the existence of a complete discrete valuation ring $W$, a ring homomorphism $\sigma:A\to W$ with $\mathfrak m_W=(\sigma\varpi)$, power series $f,u,v\in W[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u,v$ units and $f\equiv X_0X_1^q-X_0^qX_1$ modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$ (the Drinfeld form [`DrinfeldCurve.LocalChart.drinfeldForm`](def/DrinfeldCurve_LocalChart.html#L18)), and a ring isomorphism
--   $$e:\widehat{\mathcal O_{X,z}}\;\xrightarrow{\ \sim\ }\;S:=W[[X_0,X_1]]/\bigl(C(\sigma(\varpi_t^{\,q+1}))\,v-f\,u\bigr)$$
--   from the adic completion of the stalk, subject to six further clauses, summarised here: (i) $e$ carries the germ of each $a\in A$ to the class of the constant $C(\sigma a)$; (ii) every level automorphism $\tau$ of $K$ attached to $\gamma^{-1}$ for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ preserves $C$; (iii) if in addition $\gamma_{11}\equiv 1\bmod\ell$, then $\tau$ is the identity on $C/y'$; (iv) for such $\gamma$ and $\tau$ acting trivially on $C/y'$ there are a ring automorphism $\theta$ of $S$ transporting the action of $\tau$ through $e$ and the germ map, fixing constants, an element $c\in W$ with $c^{q+1}\equiv1$ and a matrix $M$ over $W$ with $M_{ik}\equiv c\,\gamma_{ik}$ modulo $\mathfrak m_W$, such that $\theta$ acts on the classes of $X_0,X_1$ by $M$ modulo the square of the ideal generated by them, with $c\equiv1$ whenever $\gamma_{11}\equiv1\bmod\ell$ and $c\not\equiv1$ whenever $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)$ and $\tau\neq\mathrm{id}$; (v) two primes of $S$ lying over $\sigma\varpi$, not containing both coordinates, with tangent directions $(a_1:b_1)$, $(a_2:b_2)$ such that $q\nmid a_1b_2-a_2b_1$, have distinct contractions to the stalk; (vi) for a prime $P$ of $S$ over $\sigma\varpi$ with tangent direction $(1:0)$ and $a\in C$, the germ of $a$ lies in the contraction of $P$ if and only if every Laurent coefficient of $a$ lies in $\mathfrak m_A$; (vii) [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L q`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) lies in $K$ and in $C$, and for a suitable $a_0\in A$ with the difference in $y'$ the image of that difference under $e$ is the class of a power series $h\in(X_0,X_1)^{e_0}$, $e_0\ge1$, whose degree-$e_0$ leading form takes unit values at all $(a,b)$ over $W$ not both in $\mathfrak m_W$ with $a^qb-ab^q\in\mathfrak m_W$.
--
--   **The pinned presentation.** Points $z$, $\varpi_z$, $y'$ as above are fixed (hypotheses `hϖz`, `hz`, `hy'`, `hss'`), with $y'=y$ (`hy'y`), together with explicit data $W_1,\sigma_1,f_1,u_1,v_1$ and $e_1:\widehat{\mathcal O_{X,z}}\cong S:=W_1[[X_0,X_1]]/(C(\sigma_1(\varpi_t^{\,q+1}))v_1-f_1u_1)$ of the same shape, for which the hypothesis `hW₁` asserts exactly the six clauses (i)–(vii) listed above (with `mkS` the quotient map and `germY` the germ map $C\to\mathcal O_{X,z}$ through $\operatorname{Spec}C$).
--
--   **Blow-up data.** The ideal $J\subseteq C$ is, by `hJ`, the intersection over all $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ and all level automorphisms $\tau$ attached to $\gamma^{-1}$ preserving $C$ of the pullback along $\tau|_C$ of the contraction, along $e_1\circ(\text{completion})\circ\text{germY}$, of the ideal of $S$ generated by the classes of $C(\sigma_1\varpi_t)$, $X_0$ and $X_1$. The $A$-subalgebra $B\subseteq K$ is, by `hB`, the $C$-algebra generated by $\{x\in K:\ x\varpi_t\in J\}$, that is $C[J/\varpi_t]$.
--
--   A valuation subring $W\subseteq K$ containing $B$ (`hBW`) is given, subject to: `hR1`, that $C\le B$ and $K$ is the fraction field of $B$; `hR2`, that $B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation over $A$ and $B/\varpi B$ has Krull dimension at most $1$; `hR3` (five clauses), that $W\cap L$ is the image of $A$, that $\mathfrak m_W$ is generated by $\varpi$, that $W$ is a discrete valuation ring, that $y$ is the contraction of $\mathfrak m_W$ to $C$, and that $W$ is the localisation of $B$ at $\mathfrak m_W\cap B$; and `hEQ` (five clauses, summarised here), that for any $\mathbb F_{q^2}$-algebra structure on the residue field $\kappa$ of $A$ there is a surjection $\rho:B\to$ [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q κ`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) with kernel $\mathfrak m_W\cap B$, compatible with constants and equivariant for the [`DrinfeldCurve.hAction`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L325) of the reduction `redQ q γ` of each $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ paired with a scalar $c\in\mathbb F_{q^2}^\times$, with $c\neq1$ when $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)$ and $\tau\neq\mathrm{id}$; that $B$ is stable under all level automorphisms attached to $\Gamma_0(M')$; that every prime of $B$ over $\varpi$ is obtained from $\mathfrak m_W$ by such an automorphism with $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$; that an element of $B$ lying in all these translated maximal ideals is divisible by $\varpi$; and that a level automorphism preserving $y$ preserves $W$.
--
--   **Cyclic and end data.** Let $n\ge1$ divide $q+1$ (`hn1`, `hnq`), let $\gamma_0\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ (`hγ₀q`, `hγ₀M`) and let $\tau_0$ be an automorphism of $K$ over $L$ which is a level automorphism at $\gamma_0^{-1}$ in the sense of [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.IsLevelAutAt L q ζ q (q^2*M') H₁`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelLevelAutAt.html#L29), i.e. on quotients $f/g$ of modular forms of level $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$ with integral $q$-expansions, $\tau_0$ induces, through any complex embedding of $L$ sending $\zeta$ to $e^{2\pi i/q}$, the weight-$k$ action of the matrix `conjElemN q γ₀⁻¹` (`hτ₀`). Assume $W$ is $\tau_0$-stable (`hτ₀W`), $\tau_0^n$ fixes $B$ pointwise (`hcyc1`), and no $\tau_0^k$ with $0<k<n$ does (`hcyc2`). Let $m\ge1$ satisfy $\varpi^m=\varpi_t\cdot(\text{unit})$ (`hm1`, `hmt`). Finally let $O\subseteq K$ be a subring satisfying the end condition `hO`: there are $a\in J$ with $a\neq0$ in $K$ such that, writing $B_a:=C[J/a]$ for the $C$-algebra generated by $\{x\in K:\ xa\in J\}$, there is a maximal ideal $P$ of $B_a$ with $O$ the localisation of $B_a$ at $P$, every element of $y$ a non-unit in $O$, and $B\not\subseteq O$; and assume $O$ is $\tau_0$-stable (`hOτ`).
--
--   **Conclusion.** Write $\widehat A$ for the $\mathfrak m_A$-adic completion of $A$, $\hat\varpi$ for the image of $\varpi$ in it, and $\mathcal U:=$ `UVCrossingModel` $\widehat A\,\hat\varpi^m=\widehat A[[X_0,X_1]]/(X_0X_1-\hat\varpi^m)$, with distinguished elements `U`, `V` and constants `const`. Then there is $\zeta_0\in\widehat A$ with $\zeta_0^{\,n}=1$ and $\zeta_0^{\,k}-1$ a unit for $0<k<n$, such that:
--
--   - $O\subseteq W$;
--
--   - $O$ is local and Noetherian;
--
--   - $C\subseteq O$;
--
--   - for $x\in L$, one has $x\in O$ if and only if $x$ lies in the image of $A$;
--
--   - every $f\in O$ is congruent to a constant: there is $a\in A$ with $a\in O$ and $f-a$ a non-unit of $O$;
--
--   and, with $\varpi\in O$, there are $c_x,c_y\in O$, a unit $u\in O^\times$, a ring isomorphism
--   $$\iota:\widehat O\;\xrightarrow{\ \sim\ }\;\mathcal U$$
--   from the $\mathfrak m_O$-adic completion of $O$, units $\gamma_U,\gamma_V$ of $\mathcal U$, an $\widehat A$-algebra automorphism $\theta_0$ of $\mathcal U$, an element $\zeta_0'\in\widehat A$ with $\zeta_0\zeta_0'=1$, and $\mathcal U$ local, such that:
--
--   1. $c_xc_y=\varpi^m u$ in $O$;
--
--   2. $\iota$ carries the image of each $a\in A$ to `const` $a$;
--
--   3. $\iota(c_x)=\gamma_U\cdot$ `U` and $\iota(c_y)=\gamma_V\cdot$ `V`;
--
--   4. $c_y$ lies in $\mathfrak m_W$ and $c_x$ does not (whenever they lie in $W$);
--
--   5. $\iota$ intertwines $\tau_0$ with $\theta_0$: for $f\in O$ with $\tau_0f\in O$, $\iota(\tau_0 f)=\theta_0(\iota f)$;
--
--   6. $\theta_0(\mathrm{U})-\mathrm{const}\,\zeta_0\cdot\mathrm{U}$ and $\theta_0(\mathrm{V})-\mathrm{const}\,\zeta_0'\cdot\mathrm{V}$ both lie in $\mathfrak m_{\mathcal U}^2$;
--
--   7. (the pin relating $\zeta_0'$ to the tangent scalar of $\tau_0$ on the Drinfeld chart) for every $c\in W_1$, every ring automorphism $\theta$ of $S$ and every matrix $Mx$ over $W_1$ such that $\tau_0$ preserves $C$, $\theta$ transports the action of $\tau_0$ through $e_1$ and the germ map, $\theta$ fixes the classes of constants, $\theta$ acts on the classes of $X_0,X_1$ by $Mx$ modulo the square of the ideal they generate, and $Mx_{ik}\equiv c\,(\gamma_0)_{ik}$ modulo $\mathfrak m_{W_1}$: for every $a\in A$ with $c\equiv\sigma_1a$ modulo $\mathfrak m_{W_1}$, the element $\zeta_0'-a$ is not a unit of $\widehat A$.
--
--   This is the local analysis, at one $\tau_0$-stable end of the blow-up of the supersingular chart of $X_{H_1}(q^2M')$, that produces a crossing (node) presentation $\widehat O\cong\widehat A[[U,V]]/(UV-\varpi^m)$ on which the chosen cyclic level automorphism acts with tangent characters $(\zeta_0,\zeta_0^{-1})$, the scalar $\zeta_0'$ being pinned to the tangent scalar read off on the Drinfeld chart. It is a step in the semistable-model computation in the $\Gamma_1(\ell)$-guarded frame, which dispenses with the hypothesis $q\ge5$, and it feeds the corresponding statement phrased for an arbitrary end.
